          {
            "type": "text",
            "title": "Counting factors",
            "body": "2³ means 2 × 2 × 2. So 2³ × 2⁴ is seven 2s multiplied together: 2⁷. Every law of indices is just counting factors in a different way."
          },
          {
            "type": "formula",
            "title": "The laws",
            "body": "aᵐ × aⁿ = aᵐ⁺ⁿ\naᵐ ÷ aⁿ = aᵐ⁻ⁿ\n(aᵐ)ⁿ = aᵐⁿ",
            "caption": "The base must be the same to add or subtract exponents."
